  "configuration_id": "config_022",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only (PCA n2000, single profile) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while both image-only models are very weak (ResNet50: 20.8%, ViT-L: 22.7%), suggesting image features carry little standalone signal. The central research question is whether multimodal fusion can combine the strong RNA signal with any complementary image information to exceed the RNA-only baseline. Uncertainty: We have zero data on whether fusion helps or hurts; image features may be too noisy to contribute, or they may capture complementary morphological information. This experiment (config_022: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat) directly tests the core multimodal hypothesis using the strongest RNA encoder (PCA n2000) paired with the best-performing image encoder (ViT-L, slightly ahead of ResNet50) and the simplest fusion (concat), keeping the profile setting at single to remain directly comparable to the config_001 baseline. If multimodal does not beat ~48.5%, we can rule out the entire multimodal branch and redirect budget to RNA encoder/aggregation improvements; if it does, it opens a rich search over fusion strategies, aggregation, and encoders. This single experiment resolves the highest-impact uncertainty in the search space."
}

